      </select>
      <p class="hint">Videos up to 60 MB (.mp4 or .webm); short reels of 5 to 15 seconds load fastest. Leave it empty to use one of your site's photos. On a computer the card fills the screen; on a phone everything stacks.</p>
    <% } else if (b.type === 'stack') { %>
      <input type="hidden" name="block_image" value="">
      <p class="hint">The small label, heading and rating line sit on the left with arrows and "1 of N" under them; the cards lie in a tilted pile on the right. As visitors scroll down through the block, the top card flies off and goes to the back, one card at a time (the arrows do the same). Put [square brackets] around heading words to color them. For anyone who turns motion off the page doesn't hold still while scrolling; the arrows still turn the cards.</p>
    <% } else if (b.type === 'nodes') { %>
      <input type="hidden" name="block_image" value="">
      <label>How the pictures change</label>
      <select name="block_side">
        <% [['auto', 'Fade to the next picture'], ['slide', 'Wipe up to the next picture'], ['still', 'Don\'t change (first photo only)']].forEach(o => { %><option value="<%= o[0] %>" <%= nodeCards.cleanSide(b.side) === o[0] ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= o[1] %></option><% }) %>
      </select>
      <p class="hint">The heading shows big, with your small words under it; words in the box above take turns on its last line. On a computer the whole block fits one screen. The cards sit in staggered columns joined by thin lines, each with its two labels above it. A card with words shows them in place of photos. Each photo card's pictures take turns, one card at a time: its own photos first, then your site's (a card with fewer than 3 photos borrows some). Put [square brackets] around heading words to color them. Visitors can pause the pictures, and they hold still for anyone who turns motion off. On phones the cards sit two across, without the lines.</p>
    <% } else if (b.type === 'beforeAfter') { %>
